# Boot keyboard: CircuitPython's usb_hid.Device.KEYBOARD (MIT), the descriptor
# the RP2040 HID board presents, with its Report ID removed -- each HID
# function is its own interface here, so no report IDs are needed, and a boot
# keyboard's reports must not carry one.
#
# Input report, 8 bytes:  [modifiers, reserved, key1..key6]
# Output report, 1 byte:  LEDs (num, caps, scroll, compose, kana)
#
# Everything after '#' is a comment; the rest is hex bytes.
05 01        # Usage Page (Generic Desktop)
09 06        # Usage (Keyboard)
A1 01        # Collection (Application)
05 07        #   Usage Page (Keyboard/Keypad)
19 E0        #   Usage Minimum (Left Control)
29 E7        #   Usage Maximum (Right GUI)
15 00        #   Logical Minimum (0)
25 01        #   Logical Maximum (1)
75 01        #   Report Size (1)
95 08        #   Report Count (8)
81 02        #   Input (Data,Var,Abs)          modifier byte
95 01        #   Report Count (1)
75 08        #   Report Size (8)
81 01        #   Input (Const)                 reserved byte
95 05        #   Report Count (5)
75 01        #   Report Size (1)
05 08        #   Usage Page (LEDs)
19 01        #   Usage Minimum (Num Lock)
29 05        #   Usage Maximum (Kana)
91 02        #   Output (Data,Var,Abs)         LEDs
95 01        #   Report Count (1)
75 03        #   Report Size (3)
91 01        #   Output (Const)                LED padding
95 06        #   Report Count (6)
75 08        #   Report Size (8)
15 00        #   Logical Minimum (0)
26 FF 00     #   Logical Maximum (255)
05 07        #   Usage Page (Keyboard/Keypad)
19 00        #   Usage Minimum (0)
2A FF 00     #   Usage Maximum (255)
81 00        #   Input (Data,Array,Abs)        six key slots
C0           # End Collection
